  {"comment": "Drifting Noise attached to a painted layer at forty pixels a second rightwards, its row pressed so Tool Options shows its panel with the time row. A shot at nought, then the scrubber moved to two seconds with control and a shot of the noise eighty pixels on, then back at nought and a shot that is the first again. Each reads two texels eighty pixels apart, so the texel at 300 at two seconds is near the texel at 220 at nought."},
